<!--
    narrowret: a call reads the narrow value its callee returns (Thumb-2).

    The image is decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/narrowret.c
    (clang for thumbv7em-none-eabi, cortex-m4, -O2), its calls
    resolved at 0x10000.  `next_byte` returns `uxtb r0, r0` and `above` a
    comparison, both zero-extended into r0 as AAPCS requires; `larger_byte`
    and `count_above` keep two of their results in r0/r5 (r6) and compare them
    at full width.  Under `decompile-all`, callees are decompiled first and
    state the narrow value they return, and the callers then hold the results
    as `unsigned char v1` and `bool v1` (`mix(v2 || v1,a0)`); with the option
    off they are `unsigned int v1`.

    THIS FIXTURE IS THE NEGATIVE CONTROL.  A callee states its return only
    after its own decompile in a whole-binary `decompile-all`
    (`kuna_narrowret::record`, called where `park_recovered_proto` is true,
    which only decompiler/crates/kuna-cli/src/decompile_all.rs sets).  This
    harness decompiles ONE function from a byte image, so nothing is stated:
    each callee still narrows its own return exactly as before (#1, #2), each
    call output stays the whole register (#3, #4, #5), and the sign-extended
    `signed_byte` result stays signed (#6), byte for byte alike in both
    passes.

    The POSITIVE witnesses run the same objects through `decompile-all`:
    tests/cli/narrowret-holds-a-narrow-call-result-narrow.json (on) and
    tests/cli/narrowret-off-keeps-the-register-wide-call-result.json (off),
    and decompiler/crates/kuna-cli/tests/narrow_ret.rs, which also compiles the
    printed C of both arms and checks it computes what the binary computes.

    Stage / sub-stage: P4 "output-prototype".  Pass 1 (default on) and pass 2
    (off) must print the same.
-->
